摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"A Rust database CLI for agents with encrypted datasources and on-demand native/JDBC workers","id":"gh:1364036006","install_available":false,"language":"Rust","name":"sqlx","slug":"OtterMind/sqlx","topics":["agent-skills","database","dsh-plugin","mcp","pi-package","sql"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"A Rust database CLI for agents with encrypted datasources and on-demand native/JDBC workers"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# SQLX"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Connect to MySQL, MariaDB, TiDB, GreatSQL, OceanBase, PostgreSQL, CockroachDB, YugabyteDB, openGauss"},{"id":"p3s2","text":", Oracle, SQL Server, ClickHouse, Trino, Presto, StarRocks, Apache Doris, TDengine, Dameng, Kingbase"},{"id":"p3s3","text":"ES, Apache Kylin, XuguDB, IBM Db2, IBM Informix, SUNDB, GBase 8s, Redis and MongoDB, or open a local"},{"id":"p3s4","text":" SQLite, DuckDB or H2 file, from your terminal or from your agent. Connections are saved encrypted, "},{"id":"p3s5","text":"one invocation runs one or more statements or commands, and the results come back complete and struc"},{"id":"p3s6","text":"vocation runs one or more statements or commands, and the results come back complete and structured."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Using an agent? See Use with your agent: install one plugin or extension and the agent calls SQLX di"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"n agent? See Use with your agent: install one plugin or extension and the agent calls SQLX directly."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Install the CLI"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Three channels, pick one: prebuilt packages from GitHub Releases, the `npx` installer, or the platfo"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"k one: prebuilt packages from GitHub Releases, the `npx` installer, or the platform install scripts."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"### macOS and Linux"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"The installer selects your platform, downloads the executable and verifies its SHA-256. It installs "},{"id":"p11s2","text":"to `~/.local/bin`; add that directory to your shell's persistent PATH. `SQLX_INSTALL_DIR` chooses an"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"other directory and `SQLX_VERSION` selects a release version."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"### Windows x64"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Run in PowerShell:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Add `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\SQLX` to your user PATH for future sessions. Neither installer overwrit"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"es an unrelated executable already named `sqlx`; use a different install directory in that case."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Prebuilt targets are macOS ARM64/x64, Linux ARM64/x64 and Windows x64; the Linux baseline is Ubuntu "},{"id":"p16s2","text":"24.04. Release users do not need Rust, Java or database drivers: database workers and a private JRE "},{"id":"p16s3","text":"are downloaded only when needed."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"### Node.js (`npx`)"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"macOS, Linux and Windows x64 with Node.js 22 or newer:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"The installer verifies the release manifest, `SHA256SUMS` and the downloaded archive before installi"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"ng. It uses the same user-level location as the platform installers and installs the Skill into `./s"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"qlx`, which no agent watches: `--target codex`, `--target claude`, `--target dsh`, `--target pi` or "},{"id":"p20s4","text":"`--target <directory>` place the Skill where it is actually discovered, and `--cli-only` installs th"},{"id":"p20s5","text":"e CLI alone. Any other first argument is run as a SQLX command instead of installing, so `npx -y @ot"},{"id":"p20s6","text":"termind/sqlx@latest mcp` starts the MCP server. Node.js is needed only by the installer, never by th"},{"id":"p20s7","text":"d/sqlx@latest mcp` starts the MCP server. Node.js is needed only by the installer, never by the CLI."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"### Updates"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"The CLI updates its own executable:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"`sqlx update install --version <version>` installs an exact stable version. Updates do not stop runn"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"ing SQL or the UI service, do not modify saved connections, and do not update Skills or plugins auto"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"matically; use `sqlx skill update` for managed Skills, and an installed UI plugin keeps the version "},{"id":"p24s4","text":"you selected (the default interface moves with the CLI release)."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Interactive use checks in the background at most once per day and only prints a notice on stderr. Pi"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"ped and CI commands skip that check, and `SQLX_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=1` disables it. Source builds and pac"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"kage-manager-owned paths keep their own installation method."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Use with your agent"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"All four are ready as soon as they are installed: the plugin or extension installs the `sqlx` CLI\nit"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"self when it is missing, so you never install it separately. Codex and Claude additionally\nrequire t"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"he CLI to meet the plugin's minimum version and refuse to start an older incompatible MCP\nserver sil"},{"id":"p27s4","text":" to meet the plugin's minimum version and refuse to start an older incompatible MCP\nserver silently."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Each of them also leaves the Skill installed, because the CLI alone gives an agent the tools but\nnon"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"e of the engine knowledge. A plugin installs the Skill into that agent's own directory on first\nlaun"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"ch when it is not there yet, and says so on stderr while it does."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"### Codex"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"The plugin starts `sqlx mcp` over MCP. Read-only operations run directly; the two execution tools (`"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"sqlx_sql_execute` and `sqlx_sql_view`) are marked destructive and Codex asks for approval by default"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"qlx_sql_execute` and `sqlx_sql_view`) are marked destructive and Codex asks for approval by default."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"### Claude Code"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"Headless runs need an explicit tool allowlist:"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"### DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"Plugins belong to a profile: install it into the profile you use, then restart dsh."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"### Pi"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"### Any other MCP client"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"A client with no plugin system takes the server straight from the published package. It installs\nthe"},{"id":"p42s2","text":" `sqlx` CLI itself on first use, so this is the whole setup:"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p44s1","text":"Point `command` at an installed binary instead to start without `npx`; a GUI application often has\nn"},{"id":"p44s2","text":"o `~/.local/bin` on its `PATH`, so give the absolute path (`~/.local/bin/sqlx` on macOS and Linux,\n`"},{"id":"p44s3","text":"%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\SQLX\\sqlx.exe` on Windows) and keep `\"args\": [\"mcp\"]`."},{"id":"p45s1","text":"Such a client receives no Skill, so its agent runs the tools without the engine recipes. Install it\n"},{"id":"p45s2","text":"where the client reads instructions from with `sqlx skill install --path <directory>`."},{"id":"p46s1","text":"SQLX is also listed in the MCP Registry as\n`io.github.OtterMind/sqlx`, which points at a container i"},{"id":"p46s2","text":"mage for clients that install from there:\n`docker run -i --rm ghcr.io/ottermind/sqlx:latest`. A cont"},{"id":"p46s3","text":"ainer reaches only the SQL-execution path\n— the credential page, the result page and the local workb"},{"id":"p46s4","text":"ench are served on the container's own\n`127.0.0.1`, and the data directory lives inside it, so mount"},{"id":"p46s5","text":" a volume at `/root/.sqlx` to keep\nsaved connections. Prefer the package above when the user should "},{"id":"p46s6","text":"type credentials or read results."},{"id":"p47s1","text":"### Skill only"},{"id":"p48s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p49s1","text":"For another agent, pass its skill directory with `sqlx skill install --path <directory>`."},{"id":"p50s1","text":"## Connections and SQL"},{"id":"p51s1","text":"### Create a connection"},{"id":"p52s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p53s1","text":"| Database | `--type` values | Execution | Required values and defaults |"},{"id":"p54s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
